+
+## Built State (F029, 2026-09-27)
+
+What exists on disk at the close of F029, built in eight rounds over two sessions on
+`feature/f029-subtree-rerun`, cut from `main` at `b2863af4`. Every DECISION named lives in
+`.agent/decisions.md`; every round's verdict in `.agent/live_review.md` or, once rotated, its
+archive.
+
+**T001 — the reset.** The prerequisite finding: a task's commit on the job branch already is the
+per-task ref, so no ref is added and retention is the branch's own (DECISION F029 D1).
+`packages/orchestration/subtree_rerun.py` names the subtree of a task (`rerun_subtree_ids`: the
+task and everything depending on it, in plan order), walks the branch from that task's commit
+(`branch_commits_since`), and refuses before touching anything, each with its own code:
+`unknown_task`, `not_worktree_mode`, `task_not_committed`, `worktree_drift` (worded as the
+checkpoints' drift message, an unreadable head counting as moved), `worktree_dirty`,
+`commit_not_on_branch`, `subtree_order`, and `interleaved`, which names every path a commit outside
+the subtree also changed and the task or commit that changed it. `apply_subtree_reset` builds the
+target tree in a private index, restores the worktree to it and lands ONE new commit with the
+trailer `Remedy-Rerun`, then proves it: the commit's tree equals the target, every path the subtree
+changed is back at its entry before the task, and, when nothing outside the subtree followed the
+task, the whole tree equals the tree before it (`exact`, and `pre_task_tree_equal` against the
+task's recorded start tree). Nothing is rewritten; the earlier attempts' commits stay on the branch.
+
+**T002 — the preparation and the command.** `prepare_subtree_rerun` admits a job that is
+`completed`, `blocked`, `paused` or `stopped` (`job_running` and `job_not_rerunnable` otherwise,
+with `model_invalid`, `job_branch_missing`, `checkpoint_object_missing` and
+`stream_archive_occupied` before the worktree is claimed), re-adds a completed job's worktree from
+its kept branch under the job's lock, resets the subtree, and folds it (`fold_subtree_rerun`):
+every subtree task that ran keeps its finished attempt as one record in its new `attempts` list,
+its `attempt` counter rises, and it returns to `pending`; a `skipped` task outside the subtree
+returns to `pending`; a `completed` job becomes `paused`. Each rerun task's stream evidence moves
+unchanged to `rerun_attempts/<task>/attempt-<n>/` in the job's evidence directory, and the job's
+new `reruns` list records the rerun with its proof and the model override beside the configured
+model, reason `human_override`. `run_job` in `packages/orchestration/pingpong_job.py` passes a
+task's `model_override` to the builder, so the run's own record names the model it ran on
+(DECISION F029 D2). `remedy job rerun-subtree <job> <task> [--model M] [--yes] [--json]`, in
+`apps/cli/commands/job_rerun_cmd.py`, prices the subtree from each task's plan band
+(`subtree_rerun_cost_estimate`, unavailable when any task lacks a priced band), shows it through
+the cost preview before anything is touched, prepares the rerun, and names the one command that
+runs it, `remedy job run <the job's id>`; the catalog marks it `is_expensive` beside `job.resume`
+(DECISION F029 D3).
+
+**T003 — the door, the fan, the control and the report.** The write door exposes
+`job.rerun-subtree` through the one function `rerun_subtree_command`, which answers
+`needs_confirmation` with the estimate and the threshold when the cost preview would ask, prepares
+only when the command returns with `confirm_cost`, and answers a refusal as a 409; the preparation
+writes the run-log event `subtree_rerun_prepared`, worded in `apps/ui/src/api/humanizeCatalog.ts`,
+and the dashboard's task item carries `attempt` and `attempts` before `origin` (DECISION F029 D4).
+The canvas chip reads `attempt <n>` from the second attempt on, after `v<n>` and "added", and the
+task's detail popover lists its attempts in `TaskAttemptList.tsx`, each earlier row opening the
+fields that changed from the attempt before (`apps/ui/src/api/attemptView.ts`, DECISION F029 D5).
+The run detail's Rerun button sends the rerun through `apps/ui/src/api/rerunSend.ts`, with an
+optional model; a cost the preview would ask about reads as one sentence from
+`apps/ui/src/api/rerunView.ts` with "Rerun anyway" and "Cancel", and a prepared rerun reads with the
+command that runs it. The final report ends a rerun task's line with ` — attempt <n>`, and with
+`, run on <model>` when it carried an override (DECISION F029 D6). Under a mission, every rerun of
+one of the mission's jobs becomes one DECISIONS item of the mission's dossier at the loop's next
+refresh, read from the job's own `reruns` record (`rerun_decision_items` and `mission_job_reruns`
+in `packages/orchestration/mission_dossier.py`, DECISION F029 D7).
+
+**Acceptance, by the test that proves it.** Pre-task tree hash equality: `TestExactResetAndProof`
+in `tests/orchestration/test_subtree_rerun.py`, and the live proof
+`tests/ui_server/test_subtree_rerun_e2e_live.py`, which runs a three-task job through the real
+command line, reruns its middle task with an override through the door and through `job
+rerun-subtree --yes`, checks the reset commit's tree against the tree before the task with git
+itself, runs the subtree again, and reads both attempts back from the job record, the moved stream
+evidence, the run log, the dashboard, the event stream, the run records and the report. The
+interleaving fixture refused with the exact files: the two interleaving tests of
+`TestExactResetAndProof`, one naming a task outside the subtree and one naming a commit without a
+task trailer by its sha, with `TestRefusalsAreSideEffectFree` in the same file proving that a
+refusal changes nothing. The fan with its verdicts: `attemptView.test.ts`,
+`buildForceBrainModel.test.ts`, `tests/ui_contracts/test_attempt_fan_contract.py` and
+`tests/ui_server/test_dashboard_task_attempts.py`. Attempt 1's evidence untouched:
+`TestPrepareSubtreeRerunEndToEnd` in `tests/orchestration/test_subtree_rerun_prepare.py` and the
+live proof's unchanged run directory. The preview and its threshold: `TestRerunSubtreeConfirmation`
+in `tests/cli/test_job_rerun_subtree.py`, `TestRerunSubtreeCommand`,
+`tests/ui_server/test_rerun_subtree_door.py` and `rerunView.test.ts`. The override in the evidence
+and the report: the live proof's run records, and `TestTheReportNamesATasksAttemptAndItsOverride`
+in `tests/orchestration/test_run_report.py`. The dossier: the four rerun classes of
+`tests/orchestration/test_mission_dossier.py`. The mutation proofs of rounds 1 to 8 are their
+`.agent/authored/f029-r<n>-mutations.py`; the attempt list, the Rerun control and its confirmation
+row were rendered headless by the reviewer at rounds 5, 6 and 7, as those rounds' ledger entries
+record.
+
+**Modules and lists (closure precondition 7).** F029 added two Python modules,
+`packages/orchestration/subtree_rerun.py` and `apps/cli/commands/job_rerun_cmd.py`, and both
+joined `tests/orchestration/import_reachability_allowlist.txt`. `subtree_rerun.py` sat in
+`ALLOWED_UNWIRED` from round 1 until round 3 wired it, and that line is gone; nothing joined
+`RESERVED_NAMESPACES`. The door's import guard gained `rerun_subtree_command` and, in
+`ACCEPTED_TRANSITIVE_FORBIDDEN`, `subprocess`. The new browser modules are `attemptView.ts`,
+`rerunSend.ts`, `rerunView.ts` and `TaskAttemptList.tsx`.
+
+**Deliberate absences.** No per-task ref and no ref-retention policy exist, because the task's
+commit on the job branch is the address. The browser prepares a rerun but never starts one: the
+run stays with `remedy job run`, which the prepared answer names. The live graph's reducer does not
+read `subtree_rerun_prepared`, because the fan draws from the dashboard. No file-level diff
+between two attempts is served; each attempt's changes stay in its own commit on the job branch. A
+rerun's dossier item ages out of the five most recent decisions the dossier renders, as every
+other decision does, while the dossier's full record keeps it.
+
+**Findings.** F029 registered R-1080 — a rerun whose worktree head could not be read escaped with
+a raw error instead of the drift refusal — and R-1081 — a failure after the reset commit could
+leave the worktree lock held; each was repaired in the round after the one that raised it and
+resolved at the next booking. No finding was open at F029's claim, and none is open at its close.
